bstemious","tags":["obsolete"]},{"word":"temperate","source":"Thesaurus:abstemious"}],"categories":["English terms with quotations","Requests for date"],"glosses":["Not given to excessive drinking of alcohol."],"id":"77e4a021-bb27-4079-9160-7074932868d0"},{"examples":[{"text":"God help me to watch and to be sober.","ref":"1678, John Bunyan, The Pilgrim’s Progress from This World, to That which is to Come: […], London: […] Nath[aniel] Ponder […], →OCLC, page 31:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[31,36]],"id":"d6c76cfa-c82f-4e6d-9d4e-119aedb2698e"},{"text":"[N]o ſober man vvould put himſelf into a danger for the Applauſe of ſcaping vvithout breaking his Neck.","ref":"1680, John Dryden, “The Preface to Ovid’s Epistles”, in Ovid, Ovid’s Epistles, […], London: […] Jacob Tonson […], →OCLC:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[5,10]],"id":"13081dc0-f535-4e8a-8933-081fbfc74216"},{"text":"Which is the finest and soberest state possible.","ref":"2005, Plato, translated by Lesley Brown, Sophist, page 230d:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[24,32]],"id":"ed7a0cb8-e770-4ef0-bab9-57d7f88cc730"}],"links":[["Moderate","moderate#English"],["realistic","realistic"],["serious","serious"],["playful","playful"],["passionate","passionate"],["cool","cool"],["self-controlled","self-controlled"]],"synonyms":[{"word":"measured","source":"Thesaurus:moderate"},{"word":"mellow","source":"Thesaurus:moderate"},{"word":"middle of the road","source":"Thesaurus:moderate","tags":["idiomatic"]},{"word":"mild","source":"Thesaurus:moderate"},{"word":"moderate","source":"Thesaurus:moderate"},{"word":"nonexcessive","source":"Thesaurus:moderate"},{"word":"nonextreme","source":"Thesaurus:moderate"},{"word":"nonfanatic","source":"Thesaurus:moderate"},{"word":"proper","source":"Thesaurus:moderate"},{"word":"reasonable","source":"Thesaurus:moderate"},{"word":"reasonous","source":"Thesaurus:moderate"},{"word":"sober","source":"Thesaurus:moderate"},{"word":"temperate","source":"Thesaurus:moderate"},{"word":"tempered","source":"Thesaurus:moderate"},{"word":"unexcessive","source":"Thesaurus:moderate"},{"word":"unextreme","source":"Thesaurus:moderate"},{"word":"abstemious","source":"Thesaurus:temperate"},{"word":"calm","source":"Thesaurus:temperate"},{"word":"collected","source":"Thesaurus:temperate"},{"word":"composed","source":"Thesaurus:temperate"},{"word":"continent","source":"Thesaurus:temperate"},{"word":"cool","source":"Thesaurus:temperate"},{"word":"dispassionate","source":"Thesaurus:temperate"},{"word":"inexcitable","source":"Thesaurus:temperate"},{"word":"imperturbable","source":"Thesaurus:temperate"},{"word":"regular","source":"Thesaurus:temperate","tags":["rare"]},{"word":"sedate","source":"Thesaurus:temperate"},{"word":"sober","source":"Thesaurus:temperate"},{"word":"steady","source":"Thesaurus:temperate"},{"word":"staid","source":"Thesaurus:temperate"},{"word":"temperate","source":"Thesaurus:temperate"},{"word":"undisturbed","source":"Thesaurus:temperate"},{"word":"unexcitable","source":"Thesaurus:temperate"},{"word":"unexcited","source":"Thesaurus:temperate"},{"word":"unimpassioned","source":"Thesaurus:temperate"},{"word":"unpassionate","source":"Thesaurus:temperate"},{"word":"unperturbed","source":"Thesaurus:temperate"},{"word":"unruffled","source":"Thesaurus:temperate"},{"word":"unstirred","source":"Thesaurus:temperate"},{"word":"unsusceptible","source":"Thesaurus:temperate"}],"categories":["English terms with quotations"],"raw_glosses":["(figurative) Moderate; realistic; serious; not playful; not passionate; cool; self-controlled."],"glosses":["Moderate; realistic; serious; not playful; not passionate; cool; self-controlled."],"tags":["figuratively"],"id":"75891e3e-405f-4af9-a804-88629713a265"},{"examples":[{"text":"Twilight grey / Had in her sober livery all things clad.","ref":"1667, John Milton, “(please specify the page number)”, in Paradise Lost. […], London: […] [Samuel Simmons], and are to be sold by Peter Parker […]; [a]nd by Rob